node_modules/
dist/

# --- secrets: broad by design ---------------------------------------------
# A NARROW list is how a real key gets committed. `.env` alone does not catch
# `.env.bak`, `.env.bak.20260627053037`, `.env.production` or `secrets.env` —
# and timestamped .env backups are an established habit on this project's
# server, so the same habit on a laptop would publish a live key to a PUBLIC
# repo that already has forks. Match everything, then re-admit the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
secrets.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
*.log
.DS_Store
autopilot/package-lock.json
